Mission Local reported that Brooke Jenkins was placed in the State Bar’s diversionary program after ethics complaints, with the records incident at its center: as an assistant district attorney, she accessed a confidential rap sheet for a case she had no connection to and emailed it to a colleague who also had no connection to the case. The story said the State Bar described participation as “best resolved” by “requiring” it.

